 "summary": "The first computer text-formatting program (MIT CTSS, 1964): lines beginning with a period are control words (.center, .space, .paragraph, .fill, .adjust) that direct a formatter producing justified, paginated manuscript output. Ported to Multics (BCPL, then PL/I), Berkeley SDS 940 and DEC systems, and the direct ancestor of roff, nroff/troff and DEC Standard RUNOFF.",
